    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Given the function \(f(x)={@fx@}\) </p>
<p><b>1. Domain:</b></p>
<p>We recall that all polynomial functions are defined on \( \mathbb{R} \).</p>
<p>The function \( f: x \mapsto {@fx@} \) is a polynomial function. Then \(Dom(f)=  \mathbb{R}  = {@oo(-inf, inf)@} \). 
<p><b>2. Range:</b></p>
<p>To find the range of this quadratic function, we will use the formula below (called canonical form) to achieve our goal.</p>
<p>We recall that, \(ax^{2}+bx+c= \displaystyle a \left( x + \frac{b}{2a} \right)^{2} - \left( \frac{b}{2a} \right)^{2}+c  \). In this case, \( a = 1 \), \( b = {@-(pm1*aa + pm2*bb)@} \), and \( c = {@(pm1*aa*pm2*bb) + cc@} \).</p>
<p>We have:</p>
<p>\( \begin{align} 
{@fx@} & = \displaystyle \left( x + \frac{{@-(pm1*aa + pm2*bb)@}}{2} \right)^{2} - \left( \frac{{@-(pm1*aa + pm2*bb)@}}{2} \right)^{2} + ({@(pm1*aa*pm2*bb) + cc@}) \quad (\text{By applying above formula})\\
& = \displaystyle \left( {@x+val_b_2a@} \right)^{2} - {@abs(val_b_2a)^2@} {@if ((pm1*aa*pm2*bb) + cc)<0 then "-" else "+"@} {@abs((pm1*aa*pm2*bb) + cc)@} \\
& = \displaystyle \left({@x+val_b_2a@} \right)^{2} {@if eval_discr<0 then "-" else "+"@} {@abs(eval_discr)@}
\end{align} \)</p>
<p>We know that; </p>
<p>\( \begin{align} 
\forall x \in \mathbb{R}, \; & \displaystyle \left({@x+val_b_2a@}\right)^{2} & \geq 0; \\
\forall x \in \mathbb{R}, \; & \displaystyle \left({@x+val_b_2a@}\right)^{2} {@if eval_discr<0 then "-" else "+"@} {@abs(eval_discr)@} & \geq  {@if eval_discr<0 then "-" else "+"@} {@abs(eval_discr)@} 
\end{align}\)</p>
<p>Since \(f(x)=y\), \( Range(f)= \{y \in \mathbb{R}, y  \geq  {@if eval_discr<0 then "-" else "+"@} {@abs(eval_discr)@} \}= {@co(yv,inf)@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
